        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-14 06:18:35.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20954 build: auto-detect o2ib on kernels without IB",
        "message": "LU-20954 build: auto-detect o2ib on kernels without IB\n\nConfiguring against a kernel without InfiniBand, such as many\naarch64 VM kernels, fails unless --with-o2ib=no is given:\n\n  configure: error: cannot compile with OpenIB gen2 headers\n\nThe --with-o2ib default is \"yes\", so it cannot be told apart from\nan explicit --with-o2ib=yes.  The in-kernel o2ib check only looks\nfor the rdma headers, which are in every kernel tree, and the gen2\ncompile test then fails as a hard error.\n\nMake the default --with-o2ib=auto.  Only build the in-kernel\no2iblnd if the kernel has CONFIG_INFINIBAND_ADDR_TRANS (which\ndepends on CONFIG_INFINIBAND).  In auto mode, build without\no2iblnd, with a warning, if neither the in-kernel nor an external\no2iblnd is usable.  A gen2 compile failure for an o2iblnd that was\nfound is still an error.  An explicit --with-o2ib=yes now fails if\nno o2iblnd can be built, instead of only warning.\n\nPass ENABLEO2IB back to configure for deb builds, so auto mode\nstays auto, and skip in-kernel ko2iblnd in the DKMS configs when\nthe kernel lacks CONFIG_INFINIBAND_ADDR_TRANS.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I7bd22ef55e43990535528d9e69cfc18bff3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
